                                                "sense_id": "51ef3902-5bee-3f27-b788-02b3f5bd48dc",
                                                "text": "To start No. S.002 effectively with a heavy train, one opens the main regulator sufficiently to move the train off very slowly. An excess of regulator opening with the by-pass valve open can cause heavy slipping; if the worst happens, the slipping continues a little longer after the regulator is closed than on an English locomotive."
